# Round 107 — disputed consequences of a uniform zero-free half-plane σ > θ = 7/8, settled

| question | answer |
|----------|--------|
| size of log ζ | Littlewood (three circles between σ = θ + δ and σ > 1): log ζ(σ+it) ≪ (log t)^{(1−σ)/(1−θ)+ε} = (log t)^{8(1−σ)+ε} |
| Lindelöf range | hence ζ(σ+it) ≪ t^ε for every σ > 7/8 (one scout said only σ > 15/16; rejected: the exponent 8(1−σ) < 1 already for σ > 7/8) |
| class numbers | effective L(1,χ) ≫ 1/log q for real χ, so h(−d) ≫ √|d| / log |d| effectively (if the Dirichlet version is uniform) |
| Linnik | least prime in a progression ≪ q^{8+ε}: weaker than Xylouris's 5 |
| M(x) | no power saving was known before (it would imply a half-plane): x^{7/8+ε} is new |
| density hypothesis below 7/8 | not implied |
| Bombieri–Vinogradov | level stays 1/2 |
| critical line (μ(1/2)) | no improvement over known bounds |
-/
